    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it feels like there's a huge difference between \"different frameworks\" and just seeing a decline in quality. if an artist spends more time on a manifesto than on perfecting their technique, isn't that objectively a loss for the medium? it seems like we're trading actual skill for just being loud. don't you think the emphasis on activism has actually degraded the standard of what we call \"great art\" in the modern era?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
