      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The perception of a \"decline in quality\" often stems from applying traditional standards of craftsmanship to a medium that has evolved to prioritize conceptual inquiry. While some argue that technical skill is irreplaceable, others contend that postmodernism redefined \"skill\" to include conceptual innovation and contextual relevance. Viewing it as a degradation implies a fixed standard of artistic greatness, whereas contemporary art often embraces hybridity where intentional rawness or didacticism can itself become the novel, valuable artistic statement.",
      "source": "target",
